# "At the beginning of combat on your turn, Oko becomes a copy of up to one target creature you control until end of turn, except
# he has hexproof." Oko is cast on turn 1. On turn 3 Bot1 casts an Ornithopter and at the beginning of combat Oko targets it and
# becomes a 0/2 Ornithopter: Bot2 can not target him with a Lightning Bolt (hexproof, a refusal paired with the Bolt that does
# target the real Ornithopter), and he is no longer a planeswalker. At the end of turn he is Oko again, with his loyalty counters.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Oko, the Ringleader
Ornithopter
Forest
Island x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Island x25

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Oko, the Ringleader.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.BeginCombat]
Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Types = Artifact; Creature
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
! Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 5
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Oko, the Ringleader.Counters.Loyalty = 3
? Bot1.Battlefield.Oko, the Ringleader.Types = Planeswalker
